==================================================
14. SUPABASE ROW LEVEL SECURITY
==================================================

Enable RLS on every user-private table.

A user can:

- Read their own data.
- Insert their own data.
- Update their own data.
- Delete their own data.

A user cannot:

- Read another user's journal.
- Read another user's urges.
- Read another user's relapse notes.
- Read another user's private reasons.
- Read another user's analytics.
- Modify another user's data.

For example:

profiles:

Users can SELECT/UPDATE only where:

auth.uid() = id

For user-owned tables:

auth.uid() = user_id

Leaderboard:

Only expose explicitly public fields.

Do NOT expose the profiles table directly to anonymous/public leaderboard queries.

Use `leaderboard_profiles` as the public-safe table.

Users can only publish their own leaderboard profile when:

leaderboard_opt_in = true.

When opt-out occurs, remove or deactivate their leaderboard profile.

